  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(Cabling conjecture). Let $K \\subset S^{3}$ be a knot and $r \\in \\mathbb{Q}$. If\n$r$-framed Dehn surgery on $K$ is not prime, then $K$ is a nontrivial cable of a knot\n$J \\subset S^{3}$ and $r$ is the slope of the cabling annulus.",
